# No Cursor co-author

Never include Cursor as a co-author on any commit.

- Do not add `Co-authored-by:` lines that name Cursor, Cursor Agent, or any
  `@cursor.com` address (any capitalization).
- Do not pass `--trailer` or use a commit template that inserts those lines.
- If a tool, hook, or template inserts a Cursor co-author, strip it from the
  message before committing. After commit, inspect `git log -1 --format=%B`
  and amend to remove it before pushing.
- Human co-authors the user requested are allowed. Cursor is not.
